# Ghostty sets TERM=xterm-ghostty. A remote box whose ncurses has never heard
# that name concludes the terminal cannot do colour, and every program
# downstream agrees. ssh-env rewrites TERM to xterm-256color for the session.
#
# Not ssh-terminfo, which looks like the more correct fix and is not: it keeps
# TERM=xterm-ghostty, and Debian's stock ~/.bashrc turns the prompt colourful
# only for `xterm-color|*-256color`. A name that matches neither leaves the
# prompt grey however good the terminfo entry is. With both features on,
# ssh-terminfo wins, so the working one has to be alone.
shell-integration-features = ssh-env
